<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103703" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχν-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is cunningly wrought, work of art,
			handiwork</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκπωμα . . , τεχνήματ᾽ ἀνδρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					36
				</span></i>
			 (where pl. is used of one thing). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a man, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανουργίας τέχνημα</span>
			<i>a masterpiece</i> of villainy, ib.<i><span class="en">
				928
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>artful device, trick</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπηλα
				προσφέρων τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				322
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλια τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1355
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχύς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				2
			</span></i> (pl.): generally, <i>device, contrivance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				319a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μνημονικὸν τ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hp.Mi.</u>
				368d
			</span></i>, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ephor.
				54J.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
